{
  "reference_answer": "Honestly, it's the freedom that gets me. When I'm on my bike, I can just weave through side streets and stop wherever something catches my eye — no timetables, no traffic jams. It's also my way of switching off after a long day; the rhythm of pedalling kind of clears my head. And since I started cycling to work instead of driving, I've noticed I'm less stressed and I sleep better. It's one of those rare things that's good for you and actually fun at the same time.",
  "reference_angle_summary": "独立主线：以“自由感 + 减压 + 实际生活改变”为个人化理由，示例不代表用户经历。",
  "takeaway_expressions": [
    {
      "expression": "the freedom that gets me",
      "meaning_zh": "最吸引我的是那种自由感",
      "why_useful": "自然表达“喜欢某事的核心原因”，比 I like it because it is free 更地道，可用于爱好、旅行、职业等话题。",
      "example": "It's the freedom that gets me — I can work from anywhere.",
      "usage_note": "口语中常用 that gets me 表示“打动我的点”。"
    },
    {
      "expression": "switching off",
      "meaning_zh": "放松、停止思考工作或压力",
      "why_useful": "高频口语短语，替换 relax，适合描述减压方式、周末活动、爱好。",
      "example": "I go for a run after work just to switch off.",
      "usage_note": "常与 after work / at the weekend 搭配。"
    },
    {
      "expression": "clears my head",
      "meaning_zh": "让头脑清醒、理清思绪",
      "why_useful": "形象且高频，用于说明运动、散步、独处等带来的心理效果。",
      "example": "A walk by the river always clears my head.",
      "usage_note": "主语通常是活动或事物，如 it / a walk / cycling。"
    }
  ]
}

